From b8a61ba3331f70924100e842fa2858ece8ebec37 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lazybrar <211365301+lazybrar@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 17:20:52 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] firmware: qcom: qseecom: add /dev/qseecom userspace
 interface

Add a misc character device that lets userspace load a trusted app, query
whether an app is loaded, send commands to it and unload it. The ioctl
numbers and structures match the downstream Android qseecom driver for
this subset, so libQSEEComAPI and the Android HALs built on it can use it
unchanged.

Request and response data is copied through TZ memory (qcom_tzmem), which
avoids the downstream ion shared buffer handling; the app image is read
from a dma-buf. Listeners (TrustZone to Linux callbacks) are not
supported yet, so apps that need them (RPMB, secure file system) do not
work.

Hidden behind CONFIG_QCOM_QSEECOM_DEV.

Signed-off-by: lazybrar <211365301+lazybrar@users.noreply.github.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
